<p>When a printer is equipped with a finisher, the printed documents can 
 be stapled in individual sets.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If the <span class="Term-Soft">Staple:</span> list 
 is grayed out, check that the optional finisher is installed on the printer 
 and selected on the <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> tab of the 
 printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>When the stapling side selected differs from the 
 binding side selected in the <span class="Term-Soft">2 sided:</span> list, 
 staple setting will be automatically set to Off. The binding side and 
 stapling side need to be consistent.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used Settings</span> 
 tab or the <span class="Term-Soft">Finishing</span> menu of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed 
 Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the stapling position in the <span class="Term-Soft">Staple:</span> 
 list.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">When this feature 
 is in use, the printed document is collated automatically.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="4">
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
